ht gradually  coming on like a dimmer like a reverse  dimmer to convince your body that it's  sunrise and that you should get up  gradually as the Sun rises and this  works even when it's pitch-black outside  there are sounds that go along with it  but this is a much less jarring way to  wake yourself up and I am so much more  rested when I wake up with a sunrise  alarm as compared to a blaring sound and  I got a better night's sleep because I  separated my cell phone from the alarm  function there is a great video on  youtube of simon Sinek where he talks  about the dumbest thing  the millennial generation does myself  included it used to be was using their  cell phone as an alarm and being too  cheap to buy a separate physical alarm I  wholeheartedly agree with them just get  some other clock radio if you want to go  the cheap route or if you want to spend  a little bit more money you can get any  number of 32 $100.00 sunrise alarms they  all seem to work pretty well a separate  alarm will allow you to get more sleep  it'll wake you up more gradually you'll  be in a better mood and you will be more  alert for your law school classes  throughout the day  studies show that a lack of sleep  prevents the ability to memorize  internalize information and remember so  just an hour of sleep more per night  alone could put you above your  classmates in law school so law school  is all about creating a competitive  advantage as compared to your classmates  these little things whether it's a  foldable book stand so you save your  neck from neck pain and allow yourself  to study just a little bit longer every  day in the library or a separate  physical alarm to get more sleep at  night and to wake up more alert these  things may not be huge advantages in and  of themselves but they compound over  time and allow you to study a little bit  longer be more alert and just be a  better law student all-around and when  you're graded on a curve as you are in  law school these little 